BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Seeds
DTSTART:20260714T013000Z
DTEND:20260714T035000Z
DTSTAMP:20260714T013000Z
UID:5NBCoNvtr6
DESCRIPTION:Duration: 122 mins (2h02m)\n\nThe Popcorn ListSeeds is a port
 rait of centennial farmers in the American South. Using lyrical black and 
 white imagery\, this meditative film examines the decline of generational 
 Black farmers and the significance of owning land.\n\nhttps://www.siff.net
 /programs-and-events/the-popcorn-list/seeds\n\nEstimated start: 18:45
LOCATION:SIFF Film Center\, 305 Harrison Street
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Summer's Camera
DTSTART:20260716T003000Z
DTEND:20260716T021000Z
DTSTAMP:20260716T003000Z
UID:IPSfP3t4LS
DESCRIPTION:Duration: 82 mins (1h22m)\n\nThe Popcorn ListSummer captures h
 er first crush through her late father’s camera—only to uncover photog
 raphs that reveal his hidden past\, sending Summer on a journey that trans
 forms her understanding of love and family.\n\nhttps://www.siff.net/progra
 ms-and-events/the-popcorn-list/summers-camera\n\nEstimated start: 17:45
LOCATION:SIFF Film Center\, 305 Harrison Street
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Trash Baby
DTSTART:20260716T023000Z
DTEND:20260716T042500Z
DTSTAMP:20260716T023000Z
UID:y2KejjvfeA
DESCRIPTION:Duration: 99 mins (1h39m)\n\nThe Popcorn ListTrash Baby is a c
 oming-of-age drama that follows 12-year-old Stevie as she navigates growin
 g up\, getting out\, and the art of finding beauty in the ugliest of place
 s.\n\nhttps://www.siff.net/programs-and-events/the-popcorn-list/trash-baby
 \n\nEstimated start: 19:45
LOCATION:SIFF Film Center\, 305 Harrison Street
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Remaining Native
DTSTART:20260721T013000Z
DTEND:20260721T031500Z
DTSTAMP:20260721T013000Z
UID:Ck1XfRWrty
DESCRIPTION:Duration: 87 mins (1h27m)\n\nThe Popcorn ListRemaining Native 
 is a coming-of-age documentary told from the perspective of Kutoven (Ku) S
 tevens\, a 17-year-old Native American runner\, struggling to navigate his
  dream of becoming a collegiate athlete as the memory of his great-grandfa
 ther's escape from an Indian boarding school begins to connect past\, pres
 ent\, and future.\n\nhttps://www.siff.net/programs-and-events/the-popcorn-
 list/remaining-native\n\nEstimated start: 18:45
LOCATION:SIFF Film Center\, 305 Harrison Street
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Granite Rapids Moon
DTSTART:20260722T013000Z
DTEND:20260722T032000Z
DTSTAMP:20260722T013000Z
UID:AoEOeejDhF
DESCRIPTION:Duration: 93 mins (1h33m)\n\nAfter receiving a cryptic card on
  the date of his daughter's ninth birthday\, a happily married man sets of
 f on a solo backpacking trip through the Grand Canyon in an attempt to fin
 d peace with a decision from his past before it unravels his future.\n\nht
 tps://www.siff.net/cinema/in-theaters/granite-rapids-moon\n\nEstimated sta
 rt: 18:45
LOCATION:SIFF Film Center\, 305 Harrison Street
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:The Fisherman
DTSTART:20260723T000000Z
DTEND:20260723T020500Z
DTSTAMP:20260723T000000Z
UID:o8j8cPGlp0
DESCRIPTION:Duration: 108 mins (1h48m)\n\nThe Popcorn ListIn this Venice F
 ilm Festival-winning feast of magical realist comedy — aging Ghanaian At
 ta Oko sets his sights on finally having his own boat and becoming the env
 y of his village\, he’ll just need help from a dead talking fish.\n\nhtt
 ps://www.siff.net/programs-and-events/the-popcorn-list/the-fisherman\n\nEs
 timated start: 17:15
LOCATION:SIFF Film Center\, 305 Harrison Street
END:VEVENT
